                                                "sense_id": "72aadec3-1ead-35fb-8ae1-84a060f6cefc",
                                                "text": "The stealthy Apaches waited until their pale-face friends were well asleep, and then with a piece of cow-hide, hard and thin, sawed out a section of the adobe wall, at the other end of the corral, and in the morning Los Americanos found themselves horseless and muleless."
